// boxcxx — <__bits/version_memory>
//
// The __cpp_lib_* feature-test macros [version.syn] owned by <memory> --
// split out for the same [support.limits.general] per-header reason as
// <__bits/version_any>/<__bits/version_bitset> -- see those files' comments.
//
// __cpp_lib_out_ptr is P1132R8's [smartptr.adapt] (out_ptr/inout_ptr).
// 202106L is the C++23 value; C++26's P2833 bumps it to 202311L (adds the
// reset(Args...)-style array uplift) -- Ф30f-1 is a C++23-only slice, so
// that bump is not implemented and this macro is pinned at 202106L.
//
// constexpr_dynamic_alloc is claimed on evidence, not on the presence of
// the constexpr keyword: allocator<T>::allocate + construct_at +
// destroy_at + deallocate round-trip inside a static_assert on this
// toolchain (cxxtest Phase131 asserts the same thing).
//
// <memory> also includes <__bits/version_atomic> (for the jointly-owned
// __cpp_lib_atomic_value_initialization) and <__bits/version_containers>
// (for the jointly-owned __cpp_lib_allocator_traits_is_always_equal).
//
// atomic_shared_ptr is P0718R2 -- atomic<shared_ptr<T>> and
// atomic<weak_ptr<T>>, both of which now park in the kernel and honour
// notify_one/notify_all instead of polling (Ф31e-d). It names only those two
// specializations; Annex D's free shared_ptr atomic functions, which the same
// step added, are not part of it.
//
// allocate_at_least is P0401R6 as C++23 shipped it: allocation_result plus
// allocator_traits::allocate_at_least plus allocator::allocate_at_least.
// There is no free std::allocate_at_least in C++23 -- [memory.syn] has no
// such declaration -- so none is provided.
//
// shared_ptr_arrays and smart_ptr_for_overwrite are claimed on the four
// allocate_shared / allocate_shared_for_overwrite array overloads that
// Ф31e-g-2 added, and on the initialisation rules going with them:
// allocate_shared now routes element construction and destruction through
// allocator_traits<A2> per [util.smartptr.shared.create]/7-8, while the
// *_for_overwrite pair default-initialises via `::new (pv) U`.
//
// Deliberately absent (see <version>'s list): start_lifetime_as's sibling
// is_implicit_lifetime (no toolchain builtin).
